From 37dc5d59f27b64637594ab9edfcd608264d24373 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dm1sh <me@dmitriy.icu>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 18:58:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Solve interactive Cloudflare challenges in a user-visible
 WebView

The headless WebView used by the Cloudflare interceptor immediately
aborts on challenges that need interaction (invisible WebView, no way to
click). Fall back to a small user-facing screen hosting the challenge
WebView after the headless attempt fails, so the person in front of the
device can complete interactive Turnstile challenges by hand.

The screen's WebView is loaded with the triggering request's headers -
most importantly its User-Agent - and shares the CF cookies with OkHttp
through the Android CookieManager, so the clearance earned by solving
here applies to the request that caused the challenge (including the
tracker API calls to domains like shikimori.rip).
